        {
          "text": "Entropy-based detection is effective only when the attacker injects a sufficiently large fraction of fake profiles.",
          "cite_keys": ["lovelace2025poison"],
          "evidence_ids": ["e-2"]
        },
        {
          "text": "At a 3% false-positive rate, the detector recalls 91% of injected profiles when the injection ratio is high enough.",
          "cite_keys": ["lovelace2025poison"],
          "evidence_ids": ["e-2"]
        },
        {
          "text": "However, once the injection ratio drops below 0.2%, recall collapses to 38%, meaning most poisoned profiles evade detection.",
          "cite_keys": ["lovelace2025poison"],
          "evidence_ids": ["e-2"]
        },
        {
          "text": "This sharp decline indicates that low-budget poisoning attacks can remain largely undetected by entropy-based methods.",
          "cite_keys": ["lovelace2025poison"],
          "evidence_ids": ["e-2"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The detector's performance is therefore highly sensitive to the attacker's injection budget, with a critical threshold around 0.2%.",
          "cite_keys": ["lovelace2025poison"],
          "evidence_ids": ["e-2"]
        },
        {
          "text": "No study has yet compared entropy-based detection with alternative detection methods on a shared benchmark at such low injection ratios.",
          "cite_keys": [],
